.TH SEMVER-FORGE 1 "2026-10-28" "semver-forge 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
semver-forge \- automatic semantic version tracking and synchronization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B semver-forge
.RI [ --project DIR ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B semver-forge
has three project commands: init, next, and sync. It initializes version tracking, determines the next Semantic Versioning increment from Git history, applies that version to configured files, and synchronizes metadata.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Inspect the project and create .semver-forge.toml. Existing version values are preserved. Conflicting recognized version sources must be resolved before initialization. Use --yes to authorize replacing an existing configuration.
.TP
.B next
Inspect commits since the last processed Git boundary. Select the highest configured impact (breaking change, feature, or fix/performance), update the canonical version source and configured targets when a change is warranted, and persist the processed commit boundary. Re-running next does not count the same commits twice.
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize configured version metadata to the canonical version. Use --dry-run to preview. Use --version VERSION to supply a different target version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --project DIR
Operate on the specified project directory. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured JSON output.
.TP
.B --dry-run
For next or sync, preview changes without writing.
.TP
.B --explain
For next, include the reason for the selected version or no-change decision.
.TP
.B --yes
For init, authorize replacing existing project configuration.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed SemVer Forge version.
.SH VERSION SELECTION
Conventional Commit types are classified by the project's .semver-forge.toml configuration. By default, breaking changes select a major increment, feat selects minor, and fix or perf selects patch. Documentation, tests, formatting, refactoring, build, CI, and chore commits are ignored by default. The highest qualifying impact wins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .semver-forge.toml
Project configuration, including the canonical version source, synchronization targets, commit rules, and processed Git history boundary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
semver-forge init
semver-forge next
semver-forge next --dry-run --explain
semver-forge sync --dry-run
semver-forge sync
.fi
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Git is required for next. Python 3.10 or later is required.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR python3 (1)
